The public statement should:
- say the Joint Venture engine is in service and paced on durability;
- give no new dates and nothing on Airbus's or Boeing's dates or rates;
- claim no share gain;
- keep any widebody line conditional on a Re-engine on the record, on Board approval and on paying after the cost of running two programmes. 'We won't do anything not profitable' stays.
